Z||000010||sqoach||07-01-2001||09:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>I sent it to nashco last week.  I've replaced dew wipes before without any major problems.  This time I couldn't get enough clearance to get to those fricking screws even with the tool.  I have no idea what I did wrong, but I'd like to get it figured out so I can replace the wipes before I have to put my door back together.  Anyone have any suggestions???<P>MM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And I think Nascho said he left the forum for a while or something. That figures  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>And you other guys need to chill out. We're just passing a tool around. What's wrong with that? So it's only $10. So what. That's gas money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Devotshka||07-01-2001||09:06 PM||||Here ya go <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/news/99oct/99oct.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/news/99oct/99oct.htm</A> <P>Just scroll down about 1/4 of the way till ya see dew wipes or my name.  If you have any problems with the instructions, just let me know.  Once you see what you are doing in there, you'll see that you can cut those instructions down to two lines:<BR> <BR> 1.Remove dewwipe.<BR> 2.Install dewwipe.<P>Its just too simple.<BR>-doug||||reg||1
