Z||000013||Black88GT||07-02-2001||06:11 AM||||I'm sorry, but using a "primitive" tool seems much easier then having to roll the window up and hold it with one hand, then having to readjust it back into the tracks blah blah blah. <P>Also those 2 screws are often not put back in when the dew wipes are replaced and I have yet to hear anything bad about it.||||reg||7
Z||000014||Devotshka||07-02-2001||04:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I'm sorry, but using a "primitive" tool seems much easier then having to roll the window up and hold it with one hand, then having to readjust it back into the tracks blah blah blah. <BR></B><BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It IS primitive... although a better word would have to be 'laughable'.  There is no need to hold the window, i made the instructions as idiot-friendly as possible (though apparently not enough).  Readjustment 99% of the time is equivalent to pushing down on the power window button or cranking the arm.  I feel sorry for people who are so closed-minded.  I used the 'special tool' once, it was awkward and really wanted to drop the screws naturally, it was just a joke.  Now, approximately 20 vehicles worth of dewstrips later, there is not enough money in the world to make me use that garbage.  <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR><B>Also those 2 screws are often not put back in when the dew wipes are replaced and I have yet to hear anything bad about it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Sure, and people drive around on 4 lug nuts without anything bad happening either, that doesn't mean its a good thing.  Why do something half-assed when you can do it right?<P><BR>Monkeyman:  If you really want to do it the right way, but are nervous, i'd be happy to walk you through the process via email or telephone.  As i said earlier, i stupid-ized the instructions so that people that love to ask questions (or defend a glorified bent screwdriver) don't have any questions left unanswered.  If you have two hands, you can do this.<BR>Let me know if you need assistance.||||reg||3
