Z||000018||Black88GT||07-02-2001||09:24 PM||||lol.  Your getting pretty worked up over dew strips and a 10 dollar tool.  Not everyone agrees with your highness on this method.<P>Just because people don't do things your way doesn't mean they are wrong, or as you put it, "laughable" or "primitive".  There are almost always 2 or more ways to do things.  I know people who sware taking the Fiero V6 engine out of the top is the best/easiest way.  I know other people who say that is "laughable" and the only non-"half-assed" way is to drop the cradle.  Neither people are closed minded or primitive, they just do things differently (yup thats right, they do things differently, IMAGINE THAT!!)<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 07-02-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000019||Devotshka||07-02-2001||09:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>(yup thats right, they do things differently, IMAGINE THAT!!)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>God, you are so uptight.  I didn't say to stop doing what you are doing, i simply corrected your erroneous reference to holding the glass, then stated an opinion and a few facts.  You'll note the opinions are in quotations to set them apart.  i *THINK* (opinion alert! opinion alert!) that that is one 'laughable' tool.  I do, there is nothing that can change my mind on that.  That it is quite primitive, that can fall either way.  But when you think about it, LOOK at the door, seriously.  There is every provision possible to get those screws without bending a screwdriver or tacking a bit to a piece of metal.  Just an opinion... Once again... little uptight there bud.  <BR>As for the facts, yes, there are two ways to do many things.  Engine out the top, engine out the bottom, whatever floats your boat.  However, i do not see how ANY person respecting their vehicle could start a job, finish it, and have 4 screws left over and NOT call it half assed.  What happens when its a little bit difficult to get your engine bolted to your tranny?  Just leave a few bolts off?  I know, its a different situation, but the fact of the matter is, if you end up with leftover pieces you didn't do it right.    <BR>I'm just helping some people out, being a friendly person that i am.  Now if you're pissed off because you spent 3 hours screwing with a bent screwdriver because you couldn't figure out how it was meant to be done, tough luck.  Fact is, its simplistic, borderline foolproof, and i'm just helping a guy out that wanted his dewstrips back on.  <BR>  Meanwhile your high and mighty self has found some reason to attack me, i see, and for that i applaude you.  You must feel SO proud of yourself, because of what?  You think rodney dickman is going to send you a free tool for defending him?  Thousands of years of evolution and this is the best you can do?  Give me a break, i certainly don't give a damn if you don't like the correct method, and i don't think any one else here really cares if you agree or disagree with me not liking that tool.  If you got so many problems that you have to vent them on threads that don't even touch the depth of whatever your issues are, you need to go cry to daddy because no one wants to hear them here.  <P>||||reg||1
